-- title:
--   Patching datum forces isomorphism and complete-intersection presentation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with finite residue field, and let $\ell$ be a natural number whose image in $\mathcal{O}$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $R$ and $T$ be commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebras and $\varphi : R \to T$ a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism. Assume there exist a nontrivial abelian group $M$ carrying an $R$-module and a $T$-module structure such that the $R$-action is the $T$-action through $\varphi$, together with an $r \in \mathbb{N}$ and a patching datum [`Algebra.PatchingDatum 𝒪 ℓ r R M`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L39): for every $n$, a level consisting of a module $N$ over $\Lambda = \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra endomorphism $\phi$ of $\Lambda$, a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \Lambda \to R$ with $\psi(\phi(X_i)) = 0$, a surjective additive map $\pi : N \to M$ satisfying $\pi(f\cdot x) = \psi(f)\cdot\pi(x)$ whose kernel is exactly $(\phi(X_1),\dots,\phi(X_r))N$, and a finite family $b_1,\dots,b_d \in N$ spanning $N$ over the image of $\phi$ whose relations $\sum_i \phi(c_i) b_i = 0$ are precisely those with all $c_i$ in the ideal generated by the $(1+X_j)^{\ell^n}-1$. The conclusion is threefold: $\varphi$ is bijective; there is such a compatible nontrivial bimodule $M$ that is moreover free over $R$, free over $T$, with zero $R$-annihilator; and there are $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ with $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n) \cong T$ as $\mathcal{O}$-algebras.
--
--   This is the output of the Taylor–Wiles patching argument in the form used at the foot of the modularity-lifting induction: the mere existence of a patching datum on some nontrivial compatible $R$-$T$-bimodule upgrades a surjection of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $R \to T$ to an isomorphism and exhibits $T$ as a quotient of a power series ring over $\mathcal{O}$ by as many relations as variables. It is invoked in the deduction of the modularity-lifting statements for Hecke algebras at level structures arising in the Fermat application, where $R$ is a deformation ring and $T$ a Hecke algebra.
-- source:
